WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.039
Each language version of a page
needs its own title and meta

2
00:00:04.039 --> 00:00:06.987
description, in that
market's search terms.

3
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.957
General Translation's gt-next
translates titles and descriptions

4
00:00:11.957 --> 00:00:12.943
with getGT.

5
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.759
In generateMetadata, getGT
returns a translation function for

6
00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:20.024
the request's locale.

7
00:00:20.424 --> 00:00:23.292
The $context option tells the
translator that the string is

8
00:00:23.292 --> 00:00:24.870
an SEO title.

9
00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:28.916
Run npx gt translate
before next build,

10
00:00:28.916 --> 00:00:31.086
and each locale gets its own title.

11
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.644
Then localize the tags
around them: Open Graph,

12
00:00:35.644 --> 00:00:39.464
canonical, hreflang, lang,

13
00:00:39.464 --> 00:00:40.751
and structured data.

14
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.703
Your team now ships
German with each release.
